  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Pharmaceutical Preparation Manufacturing (NAICS 325412) shows $13.2B in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. The market recorded 14,748 awards with an average award size of $892K, and obligations were up 0.5% year over year. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the dominant buyer, obligating $12.3B. McKesson Corporation is the dominant vendor, receiving $12.3B in obligations. Fiscal-year obligations varied: FY21 was $19.5B, FY22 was $34.4B, FY23 was $12.8B, FY24 was $10.1B, FY25 was $13.1B, and FY26 is $13.2B. Other buyers with meaningful FY2026 to date obligations include the Department of Health and Human Services with $612M and the Department of Justice with $178M. Other top vendors in FY2026 to date include EMERGENT BIOSOLUTIONS CANADA INC with $118M and PHLOW CORP. with $105M. All figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated is buying in NAICS 325412?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $12.3B, which makes the buying highly concentrated. The Department of Health and Human Services obligated $612M, and the Department of Justice obligated $178M. The remaining listed agencies each obligated $58.8M or less in FY2026 to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who captures the largest shares of obligations?",
        "body": "MCKESSON CORPORATION received $12.3B in obligations and is the largest vendor by a wide margin. EMERGENT BIOSOLUTIONS CANADA INC received $118M and PHLOW CORP. received $105M. Several other top vendors received between $37.5M and $105M in FY2026 to date."
      }
    ]
  },
